{"id": "EUVD-2026-103910", "enisaUuid": "db592ae9-6c60-38c5-aa08-28e615e34ce0", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\niio: trigger: cancel reenable_work before freeing trigger\n\niio_trigger_notify_done_atomic() defers ->reenable() into\ntrig->reenable_work on the system workqueue, and the worker dereferences\nthe owning trigger through container_of().  Nothing cancels this work\nbefore iio_trig_release() frees the trigger, so a worker armed by the\nlast in-flight IRQ can outlive the free and touch freed memory.\n\nCancel it at the top of iio_trig_release(), which every free path\nreaches through the device core's final put_device().\n\nFound by an in-house static analysis tool.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:44:07", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:55:23", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ac5d26a46c90ff61fd574eff4e8f0d71c905828a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cf513df1a2c75566cdc802d9da47f62e8d6cfd18", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e64703280ce7a23a43c27efebeb7da457c88bf5c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/882d0011c59ff8ac15188ec9ce071399ecfa10ad", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2a57b9246cecd5dd797a42eb310d6c8816f26d9e"], "aliases": ["GHSA-6556-hh6q-qw3c", "CVE-2026-98656"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "12b82e1e-538f-391d-82be-97b0d6fa0e06", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.56"}, {"id": "14ce3f90-a084-397c-90c2-e1696d009374", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a18aeac73c0f692ba40964f5f56e182312ae843b"}, {"id": "1cbf67ce-4d82-3168-8afa-961c8d6ec019", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "3be1fb11-a3d1-388c-97ad-a05a9d562647", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.15.17 <5.16"}, {"id": "442d175c-ca2e-3c71-ae4b-4d4565d7778a", "product": {"n